ccsd superintendent dr jarrah is giving  his executive team raises totaling more  than 400 thousand dollars this decision  is getting strong criticism for many  teachers support staff and  administrators kate houston live in  studio tonight kate those who you spoke  with are concerned about the timing of  this and the reasoning behind it  yes this comes less than a week after dr  jarrah was fired from his position by  the board of trustees and as the school  district deals with hundreds of  vacancies one educator tells me seeing  executives getting a raise of this  magnitude is a slap in the face it kind  of makes me feel like i'm not i'm not  worth anything to the school district  frustrations are growing as teachers  learn of a sharp salary increase for 15  executive positions compared to the 3  percent raise they received we venture  so much with ccsd it's almost like  another kick when we're already down in  a letter to the school board dr jarrah  says this will help them compete for and  retain talent the largest raise nearly  45 thousand dollars will go to the chief  financial officer i think it's shocking  and to think that the taxpaying public  has to support that is just  unconscionable stephen augsburger  executive director of the school  administrators union says raises of this  magnitude are usually tied to  performance results but that's not the  case for ccsd test scores  and student achievement it's in the tank  and we are mired in the bottom scores of  the country augsburger notes those  receiving raises also signed a letter to  the school board expressing their  support of dr jarrah ahead of his firing  and he's calling on school trustees to  take action then they need to give clear  direction to a superintendent who's been  terminated and has 30 days to exit they  cannot continue to allow him with  operational authority and  decision-making authority because what  he just did demonstrates that he cannot  be trusted  school board president linda cavazos  weighed in on twitter she says the memo  from jarrah was unexpected and further  review of these raises is possible  cavazos voted to fire jarrah last week  now i did reach out to the school  district many times to get some  questions answered and i have not yet  heard back
 

